  m_text: 'Once when I was six years old I saw a magnificent picture in a book, called
    True Stories from Nature, about the primeval forest. It was a picture of a boa
    constrictor in the act of swallowing an animal. Here is a copy of the drawing.


    In
    the book it said: "Boa constrictors swallow their prey whole, without chewing
    it. After that they are not able to move, and they sleep through the six months
    that they need for digestion."


    I pondered deeply, then, over the adventures
    of the jungle. And after some work with a colored pencil I succeeded in making
    my first drawing. My Drawing Number One. It looked like this:


    I showed
    my masterpiece to the grown-ups, and asked them whether the drawing frightened
    them.'
